EcdsaMethodVerifyKeyTest
├── when the guardian key signs the digest
│   └── it should return the verify selector
├── when the guardian key signs a personal message of the digest
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the guardian key signs another digest
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when another key signs the digest
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the signature carries the high s half
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the recovery byte is outside its two legal values
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the signature halves are zero
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the proof is the abi encoded signature
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the proof is the compact signature
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the proof carries a trailing byte
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the proof is empty
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the config is the zero address
│   └── it should not return the verify selector
├── when the config carries a trailing word
│   └── it should answer one word that is not the verify selector
├── when the config is shorter than one word
│   └── it should answer one word that is not the verify selector
└── when the config word carries nonzero upper bytes
    └── it should not return the verify selector
